    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0590" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/31: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-13T09:00:00+03:00">July 13, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1221. General Maxwell<anchor n="37" xml:id="d691-f1"/> informs me that he has
                    suggested to War Department that General Spalding<anchor n="38" xml:id="d691-f2"
                    /> who is proceeding to this area be requested to cause a survey to be made of
                    possible defense and denial measures applicable to the oil companies at Bahrein
                    and in Saudi Arabia which have recently been the subject of an informal
                    investigation by Lieutenant Commander Lockard, United States Naval Observer at
                    Basra.</p>
                <p>As Department is aware this question has been the subject of messages from this
                    Legation and the Legation at Jidda and in view of fact that any action along
                    this line may involve presence in Saudi Arabia of American experts I urge that
                    Moose be kept informed of developments in order that he may be in position to
                    give advice and recommend measures with a view to minimizing danger of arousing
                    Saudi Arabian susceptibilities at this time.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Jidda.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d691-f1" n="37" xml:id="d691-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Russell L. Maxwell, in command of American Forces in the Middle East
                    with headquarters at Cairo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d691-f2" n="38" xml:id="d691-f2-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. Sidney P. Spalding.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
